BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Navy Week at Lake Champlain Maritime Museum
DTSTART:20260828T100000
DTEND:20260828T160000
DTSTAMP:20260825T114929Z
UID:0b6bc766fe29842a89eadfc8804fa2@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:As part of the 250th commemoration\, Lake Champlain Maritime M
 useum will partner with the United States Navy during their inaugural “N
 avy Week” in Vermont. As part of the celebration\, the US Navy\, Naval H
 istory and Heritage Command\, and the United States Undersea Museum will b
 ring a week of free educational programming to our community at the Museum
 . On August 26\, Beth Sanders\, Collections Manager\, U.S. Naval Undersea 
 Museum\, and Blair Atcheson\, Program Analyst\, Underwater Archaeology Bra
 nch will speak on the collaboration which took place to recover\, restore
 \, and share a Howell torpedo during our Deep Dives free lecture series. V
 isitors aboard our Shipwreck Tour on August 27 can connect with nautical a
 rchaeologists from the Navy History and Heritage Command. And on Friday\, 
 August 28\, Storytime will feature a very special guest: Commander Bond\, 
 the PTSD dog (pictured below). The rest of the week will feature displays 
 and interactives provided by the Navy and staffed by members of the NHHC t
 o highlight the history of the Navy and their continued commitment to conn
 ecting with American communities.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Lake Champlain Maritime Museum\, 4472 Basin Harbor Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/navy-week-
 at-lake-champlain-maritime-museum-19-08-2026-15-50-32
END:VEVENT
